    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule as a small, cohesive step in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, mirroring the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` pattern to keep structural impact minimal \u2014 no existing function was modified.\n\n**New files (each a small, single-method unit):**\n- `EnsureUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 after `NormalizeEmail` lower-cases the request email, this step scans existing owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a case-insensitive email match. Absent/blank emails pass through.\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it flows through the `throws` clause).\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 Conflict`.\n- `...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the escalation to the handler.\n\n**One-line-per-step edit** to `owners.POST.yml`: inserted `ensureUniqueEmail` between `normalizeEmail` and `normalizeAddress` (under the same `transaction` governance), so it runs after the email is normalized to lower case.\n\nThe `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
